{%- comment -%}
  Should this nav link be hidden? Echoes '1' when it should, nothing when it
  should not. The caller wraps the link in {%- unless -%}.

  THE RULE: hide a collection link only when we positively know the collection
  has no products published to the Online Store. `all_products_count == 0` is
  that positive knowledge; a nil count is NOT zero. So a link to a handle this
  theme does not recognise (/collections/all, a collection created after the
  last generator run, a preview fixture) renders as it always did, and the only
  thing that ever disappears is a category we can see is empty.

  Decided at render time on purpose. taxonomy.json stays the complete map of the
  shop; this only decides what is worth showing today, so a collection comes
  back by itself the moment a product is tagged into it. Nothing to regenerate,
  nothing to remember.

  Non-collection links are never hidden. /pages/brands is a page, and a page has
  no product count — passing its URL here must not make it vanish.

  Accepts (one of):
    handle — a collection handle
    url    — any link URL; the handle is read out of it when it is a /collections/ one

  Usage:
    {%- capture nh -%}{%- render 'nav-hide', url: link.url -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- unless nh == '1' -%}<a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title }}</a>{%- endunless -%}

  The generated nav (snippets/mega-menu, mobile-nav, category-chips) spells the
  same test inline rather than calling this snippet — 178 render tags per page
  is a cost with nothing to show for it, and those files are written by
  setup/gen_mega.py and setup/gen_category_nav.py, where the rule lives once in
  Python. If you change the rule here, change it there. Both are checked by
  setup/verify/nav-empty.py.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign nh_handle = handle
  if url != blank and url contains '/collections/'
    assign nh_handle = url | split: '/collections/' | last | split: '?' | first | split: '#' | first
  endif
  if nh_handle != blank and collections[nh_handle].all_products_count == 0
    echo '1'
  endif
-%}
